#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:201
msgid "{conversation} > {block} > line {line}"
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:208
msgid "This line held %d commands, which Candy DE 1.1.3 ran one after the other. Each is now a line of its own, and the line numbers of Jump, Bridge and choice targets in this block were updated."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:222
msgid "%s isn't the last command of its 1.1 line, so Candy DE 1.1.3 ignored it: the last command decided what came next. In 1.2 it does what it says."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:245
msgid "Two commands here become %s, and a condition can only hold it once. Only the last one was kept."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:255
msgid "Two commands here act on {entry}, which a single {command} can't do: only the last one was kept. Move one of them to a line of its own."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:258
msgid "Several commands here became one %s. Candy DE 1.1.3 ran them one after the other; 1.2 starts them together, then waits. If an earlier one waited, move it to a line of its own."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:287
msgid "The key \"%s\" isn't a command, so Candy DE 1.1.3 ignored it. It was left out (the backup still has it)."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:381
msgid "Candy DE 1.1.3 had no {old} command, so this line did nothing. It was kept as {new}."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:513
msgid "\"{text}\" read a reference stored in a variable. In 1.2 a stored reference is only read if it starts with {expression}: convert the value stored there too (\"{expression}€score\", not \"€score\")."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:723
msgid "ForceBubbles was -1 (never bubbles), which 1.2 doesn't have: Dialogue_Mode is left unset (\"null\"), so the line uses its engine's mode, speech bubbles included. To keep it out of bubbles, set its Dialogue_Mode (Box, say)."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:734
msgid "TTS was on (1). 1.2 needs the TTS mode itself: %s, your engine's, was written. Check it if your engines use different modes."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:759
msgid "Voice is a full path. 1.2 adds the variation's folder to it for every variation but Default (res://X/French/hello.ogg). Set voice_fallback_language to 'Default' in Candy_Properties.gd to fall back on the file given."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:837
msgid "Variation %s is empty. In 1.1.3 picking it skipped the line; 1.2 never picks an empty variation."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:905
msgid "The word substitution \"%s\" picks its category by number. In 1.1.3 the number counted the word group's case rule too; if the group has one, lower the number by 1."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1011
msgid "Name translated its value through the table %s, which 1.2 no longer does. Translate it with a translate() expression instead."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1013
msgid "Name translated its value through display_names before writing it to %s. 1.2 only translates DisplayName and ShortName, when they're displayed."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1129
msgid "{first} and {second} never worked in Candy DE 1.1.3, so the line left them on screen. It was set to \"0\" to keep that: set it to \"1\" to clear them."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1131
msgid "%s never worked in Candy DE 1.1.3, so the line left them on screen. It was set to \"0\" to keep that: set it to \"1\" to clear them."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1184
msgid "Loops %s fired once in Candy DE 1.1.3; 1.2 reports it and fires once. Write 1."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1209
msgid "This choice starts disabled and has a Setup. Candy DE 1.1.3 ran its Setup with the menu's; 1.2 runs it when Choice_Status enables the choice."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1231
msgid "This choice's Finish is {type} with no target, which did nothing in Candy DE 1.1.3: the menu stayed open. {effect}"
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1242
msgid "In 1.2 it ends the dialogue."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1244
msgid "In 1.2 it closes the menu."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1245
msgid "In 1.2 it closes the menu and carries on after it."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1260
msgid "{key} \"{value}\" isn't a mode. Candy DE 1.1.3 then changed everything (or, for Menu_Mode, nothing); 1.2 changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1273
msgid "A relative Loops (%s) stopped at -1 (forever) in Candy DE 1.1.3; in 1.2 it stops at 0 (no loops left), and leaves a timer looping forever as it is."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1282
msgid "This block is a timer's Timeout. Candy DE 1.1.3 counted the timeout after it, so Loops {loops} gave one firing fewer: {result} was written to keep that."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1284
msgid "This block is a timer's Timeout. If this Loops (%s) is that timer's, Candy DE 1.1.3 gave it one firing fewer: lower it by 1."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1286
msgid "A timer that had fired all its loops ran once more when restarted in Candy DE 1.1.3; in 1.2 it doesn't start. Add \"Loops\": \"+1\" to keep that."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1352 Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1395
msgid "Box and Portrait differ. The portrait is part of the dialogue box in 1.2, so they move together, as Box says."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1386
msgid "%s was a media player of Candy DE 1.1.3 that 1.2 no longer has, so this line has no player to act on."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1472
msgid "A still image on an Image player never showed in Candy DE 1.1.3 (its file path was built wrongly). In 1.2 it does."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1476
msgid "A still image with no Duration stayed up for as long as the player's last image did in Candy DE 1.1.3. In 1.2 it stays until it's stopped: give it a Duration."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1489
msgid "Volume %s was read as no change by Candy DE 1.1.3. In 1.2 it changes the volume."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1514
msgid "PEffect was the portrait's effect player in Candy DE 1.1.3. It's part of the dialogue box in 1.2, and no longer a media player: this line has no player to act on."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1542
msgid "The effect stops on its current frame, as in Candy DE 1.1.3. New in 1.2: Stop_Frame \"Clear\" plays the effect's RESET animation, if it has one, then stops."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1573
msgid "Layers was empty, which meant every layer in Candy DE 1.1.3. 1.2 needs each layer named: give your background scene's layers in the Dialogue Converter, or add them here."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1594
msgid "BG with no layer did nothing in Candy DE 1.1.3."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1597
msgid "BG took a single layer in Candy DE 1.1.3, so \"%s\" was looked up as one layer and failed. Now it's one layer of that name: split it into several if they were meant."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1666
msgid "Effects was empty, so Candy DE 1.1.3 played every animation of the library. 1.2 needs each effect named: add them."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1668
msgid "Effects was empty, which meant every effect playing in Candy DE 1.1.3. 1.2 needs each effect named: add them."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1670
msgid "Wait -1 waited until the effect's loops were done in Candy DE 1.1.3. 1.2 has no such value: write the number of loops to wait for."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1699
msgid "f= counted at 30 frames per second in Candy DE 1.1.3. 1.2 counts the media's own frames."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1710
msgid "Stop frame {frame}: Candy DE 1.1.3 went back to the first frame on an animation folder, and sought to {frame} / 30 seconds on a video. 1.2 goes to that frame, counted from 1. Check it if the layer or bust is either."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1729
msgid "This wait lasted until the layer's playback was done in Candy DE 1.1.3: Wait_Loops %s, its Loops, keeps that."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1731
msgid "This wait lasted until the bust's playback was done in Candy DE 1.1.3: Wait_Loops %s, its Loops, keeps that."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1735
msgid "This wait lasted until the layer's playback was done in Candy DE 1.1.3, which 1.2 can't say. Write the number of loops to wait for."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1737
msgid "This wait lasted until the bust's playback was done in Candy DE 1.1.3, which 1.2 can't say. Write the number of loops to wait for."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1745
msgid "Actors was empty, which meant every actor on a bust in Candy DE 1.1.3. 1.2 needs each actor named: add them."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1763
msgid "1.2 counts this wait from the start of playback, which may begin before the Join effect: the line may move on sooner than in Candy DE 1.1.3."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1843
msgid "CS_Move runs a script of yours for each target in 1.2: write your 1.1 movement code as a script in Candy DE's Scripts/Move_Events folder, and name it in each target's Movement. The line's 1.1 keys were kept on each target."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1857
msgid "Candy DE 1.1.3 didn't read roles on CS_Anim commands: %s was looked up as a node of that name. In 1.2 it's the actor in the role."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1866
msgid "Candy DE 1.1.3 waited for Wait loops, then Time more. 1.2 waits until Wait_Loops x length + Wait_Time from the start: check the timing."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1894
msgid "No markers: the line did nothing in Candy DE 1.1.3."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1910
msgid "More targets than markers: Candy DE 1.1.3 left out %s, and so does the converted line."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1927
msgid "Several scenes had no name, which 1.2 can't hold: {scene} was named {name}."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1950
msgid "{conversation} > {block} > line {line} (in 1.2)"
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:1996
msgid "The target {conversation} > {block} isn't in this file. Candy DE 1.1.3 skipped a target that didn't exist; 1.2 ends the dialogue. Check it exists in the dialogue this runs in."
msgstr ""

#: Core/dialogue_converter.gd:2005
msgid "No LM line named {line} in {conversation} > {block}. Candy DE 1.1.3 went to the block's first line; 1.2 ends the dialogue."
msgstr ""

